Summary: stress sewing for relief

I made a box-tee from the Allwell pattern today! I was searching on Everlane for a crop top and then I realized that I have the pattern for such a top that I want. The shirt itself only took about 2 active hours. I was mostly distracted by work.

[Insert some sort of work-ramble...]

I made a shirt today because stress-sewing was exactly what I needed to break the cycle of negative thoughts. I am easily sucked into the troubles of my mind. I need these activities to put me back into reality and ground my mind with my body.

I am pretty good at sewing once I understand a pattern. Not that it's a fail-proof activity. It's just got some easy parts to it or rather - it has some simplicity to it that I find rewarding when I feel otherwise incapable. It's like saying "yes, you can do stuff. You just need a break once in a while." or "you need regular breaks to keep a steady pace."